# Registry block media (images & video)

Use this when a block needs bundled raster images (PNG, JPG, WebP) or video (MP4, WebM). Most blocks (navbars, SVG-only sections, etc.) do not need this.

## Consumer install (shadcn add)

One command for consumers:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add "https://uiception.com/r/<block-id>.json"
npm run dev
```

On first `next dev` or `next build`, `instrumentation.ts` dynamic-imports `setup-uiception-media.mjs`, which:

1. Patches `next.config.mjs` to call `ensureUiceptionBlockMedia()` at build time (once).
2. Patches `package.json` to add a `prebuild` script: `node lib/uiception-media/fetch-uiception-media.mjs`.
3. Reads every `lib/uiception-media/manifests/*.json` manifest and downloads any missing binaries into `public/`.

Tests in `registry-shadcn-media-install.test.ts` and `registry-block-media.test.ts` guard this flow.

## Authoring: adding media to a block

### 1. Add a `media-manifest.json` source file

Create `registry/new-york/blocks/<block-id>/media-manifest.json` — a JSON array of `{ target, url }` pairs:

```json
[
  {
    "target": "public/images/blocks/<block-id>/<block-id>-bg.png",
    "url": "https://uiception.com/images/blocks/<block-id>/<block-id>-bg.png"
  }
]
```

- `target` — path relative to the consumer's project root (under `public/images/blocks/` or `public/videos/blocks/`)
- `url` — public URL shadcn will record for deferred download (always `https://uiception.com/<target minus "public/">`)
- The binary asset **must exist on the authoring disk** at `target` or the tests will fail.

### 2. Declare the registry dependency

In `registry.json`, add to the block's `registryDependencies`:

```json
"https://uiception.com/r/uiception-media-fetch.json"
```

This installs `instrumentation.ts`, `fetch-uiception-media.mjs`, and `setup-uiception-media.mjs` into the consumer's project.

### 3. Do NOT add binary file stubs

Do **not** list `public/images/…` or `public/videos/…` entries in `registry.json` — `shadcn build` cannot embed binaries as UTF-8. The `media-manifest.json` source file is the only artefact needed; `shadcn build` embeds it as text at `lib/uiception-media/manifests/<block-id>.json` inside the built `public/r/<block-id>.json`.

### 4. `post-registry-build.mjs` is a no-op

The post-build script no longer patches anything. All four concerns it previously handled (stripping binary stubs, generating pending manifests, setting `installUrl`, injecting the registry dep) are now handled in source. Do not add new logic there.

## Where assets live

**Images**

```
public/images/blocks/<block-id>/
  <block-id>-bg.png
  avatar_1.png
```

**Video**

```
public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/
  screen-demo.mp4
```

## Key files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `registry/new-york/blocks/<block-id>/media-manifest.json` | Source manifest — authored, committed, embedded by shadcn build |
| `registry/new-york/blocks/uiception-media-fetch/instrumentation.ts` | Entry point — dynamic-imports `setup-uiception-media.mjs` on first boot |
| `registry/new-york/blocks/uiception-media-fetch/setup-uiception-media.mjs` | Patches `next.config.mjs` + `package.json`, then calls `ensureUiceptionBlockMedia` |
| `registry/new-york/blocks/uiception-media-fetch/fetch-uiception-media.mjs` | Reads `lib/uiception-media/manifests/*.json` and downloads missing binaries |
| `lib/registry-install-media.ts` | Helpers: `pendingManifestFiles()`, `installCommandWithMediaFetch()` |
| `tests/registry/post-registry-build.mjs` | No-op — kept so package.json prebuild script entry doesn't need changing |
